# (build 104) The save's named places win over raw_c600: a hand-edited
# telepipe_lands_at is where the Telepipe goes.
#
# routes/saves/telepipe_edited.json is jet_scooter.json (a Visiphone save
# on Motavia, 89,116, on foot) with two fields added by hand:
# "last_save": { "planet": "Motavia", "by_visiphone": false } and
# "telepipe_lands_at": { "map": "Zema", "x": 368, "y": 192 } -- the cell
# under Zema's Data Memory door. Its raw_c600 still says a Visiphone save
# made on Dezolis.
#
# ItemAction_Telepipe (ps2.asm:14492) on Motavia: the last save made on
# Dezolis goes to Paseo by the Central Tower's door (y $100, x $1F0); made
# with the Visiphone, to Paseo under the Data Memory's door (y $80, x
# $110); otherwise to the last save's own place ($C646-$C64A, loc_9E86).
# Before build 104 the loader read only raw_c600, so the pipe went to
# Paseo 31,16; now the fields decide: Zema 23,12.

start slot 1 routes/saves/telepipe_edited.json
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait screen level
wait idle
expect level $00 89 116
give Telepipe 2
press c                      # the Telepipe: ITEM, Rudo, slot 6, USE
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press down
wait ticks 3
press down
wait ticks 3
press c
wait idle
press down
wait ticks 3
press down
wait ticks 3
press down
wait ticks 3
press down
wait ticks 3
press down
wait ticks 3
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
expect script $0012          # "... body feels very light."
wait screen level
wait idle
expect level $07 23 12       # Zema, as telepipe_lands_at says
shot 01_zema
expect no-stderr not a map
